# rommd local daemon — test requests
# Works with httpyac, VS Code REST Client, or JetBrains HTTP Client.

@base = http://localhost:7497

# ── Health ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

###

# ── Emulators ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### List emulators
GET {{base}}/emulators

###

# ── Status ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Status
GET {{base}}/status

###

# ── Launch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Launch Kings Field
# Fetches ROM metadata from RomM, downloads if not cached, then starts DuckStation.
# Replace rom_id with the actual ID from your RomM instance.
POST {{base}}/launch
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rom_id": 195,
  "emulator": "duckstation"
}

###

### Launch Kings Field with profile
# The disc serial is auto-derived from SYSTEM.CNF or DuckStation's gamelist.cache.
POST {{base}}/launch
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rom_id": 195,
  "emulator": "duckstation",
  "profile": {
    "overlay": {
      "GPU.ResolutionScale": "3",
      "GPU.PGXPEnable": "true",
      "CPU.OverclockEnable": "true",
      "CPU.OverclockNumerator": "200",
      "CPU.OverclockDenominator": "100"
    }
  }
}

###

### Launch from local path
# Skips RomM entirely — useful for ROMs you already have on disk.
POST {{base}}/launch
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rom_id": 195,
  "emulator": "duckstation",
  "local_path": "/Users/arseen/Roms/psx/Kings Field (USA).iso"
}

###

### Launch Mario vs. Donkey Kong (mGBA)
# rom_id 20 — single .gba file, no serial, save named after ROM filename stem.
POST {{base}}/launch
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rom_id": 20,
  "emulator": "mgba"
}

###

### Launch Mario vs. Donkey Kong with profile (mGBA)
# 2× window size (960×640) + full GBA color correction.
# Color correction makes the palette look as it did on original GBA hardware —
# immediately noticeable: warmer shadows, less washed-out highlights.
POST {{base}}/launch
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rom_id": 20,
  "emulator": "mgba",
  "profile": {
    "overlay": {
      "ports.qt.width": "960",
      "ports.qt.height": "640",
      "ports.qt.colorCorrection": "2",
      "ports.qt.interframeBlending": "1"
    }
  }
}

###

# ── Snapshot ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Snapshot running DuckStation game
# Reads the per-game gamesettings for whichever DuckStation game is currently
# running, cleans it, and returns a ProfileBlob suitable for saving to RomM.
POST {{base}}/snapshot
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "emulator": "duckstation"
}

###

### Snapshot running mGBA game
# Returns the full mGBA config.ini as a flat overlay — useful as a base for
# building or diffing profiles.
POST {{base}}/snapshot
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "emulator": "mgba"
}

###

# ── Stop ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Stop by PID
# Get the PID from the /launch or /status response.
POST {{base}}/stop
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pid": 12345
}

###

### Stop all
POST {{base}}/stop
Content-Type: application/json

{}

###
